      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Incorporating \"informal liquidity\" indicators as primary weight drivers can indeed improve the predictive capabilities for a \"proxy-first\" architecture. To prevent losing \"alpha,\" the balance between physical commercial indicators and risk assessment can be structured using a tiered weighting approach where these proxies have high initial importance. However, this direct approach must be tempered by a feedback mechanism that dynamically adjusts the weights based on real-time backtesting performance, ensuring the model remains sensitive to actual market conditions without overfitting to historical patterns. Incorporating machine learning algorithms that adapt to time-series data could help refine the model, allowing it to learn the optimal balance between various commercial markers and risk scores. Careful validation and stress-testing with historical and contemporary datasets are essential to ensure the model's robustness and to avoid any unintended bias or lost signals.",
